# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Lecture 46 vignette pool B -- macrocytic anemia and folate (s38-42), vitamin B12 and pernicious anemia (s43-50),
anemia of chronic kidney disease (s52-53, s106), aplastic anemia (s55-58, s106) and leukopenia / neutropenia
(s59-60). Every slide in range was viewed at 1920 px.

KEYS ARE WRITTEN SHORT ON PURPOSE -- detail lives in the explanation.
EXPLANATIONS follow tools/question_writing/EXPLAIN_DEEP.md: the key names the decisive clue and the slide fact;
each wrong choice says why it fails for THIS patient, the replacing fact, and a "Tell:".

Real-exam item types carried here: absolute neutrophil count worked from a white count and a differential that
includes bands, then classified (s59; lead "classify", numeric options ascending); febrile neutropenia management
(s60); folate before B12 is evaluated (s49); methotrexate / metformin and folate deficiency (s42); chloramphenicol
in a patient with aplastic anemia (s57); an offending drug in leukopenia (s60); erythropoiesis-stimulating agent
and blood pressure monitoring in chronic kidney disease (s53, s106).

Normal ranges: the deck gives only the red cell indices (s7: mean corpuscular volume 80-100 fL); every other range
in parentheses is a conventional laboratory range used to make the stem readable, never a keyed fact.
Deliberately NOT keyed: any dose (s49); iron versus erythropoiesis-stimulating agent ORDER in kidney disease (s53
lists both as "consider"); which specific drug causes neutropenia (s59 says only "medications/chemotherapy"); the
s55 incidence figures.
"""
import os, sys
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
